        "original_id": "48eefd43-5af4-5701-a5b7-8d32981d51a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Seal Islands, Suisun Bay, Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta, Contra Costa County, Benicia, Concord, California\n- Organizations: Concord Naval Weapons Station, Port Chicago Naval Magazine\n- Topics: Military bases, World War II armament storage\n\nFacts:\n- In 1942, Concord Naval Weapons Station was established as a military base north of Concord, California, on the shore of the Sacramento River where it widens into Suisun Bay.\n- During World War II, Concord Naval Weapons Station functioned as an armament storage depot that supplied ships at Port Chicago.\n- Seal Islands are a pair of islands in Suisun Bay at the mouth of the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta in Contra Costa County, California.\n- Seal Islands are 10 kilometers east of Benicia and 500 meters offshore from the former Concord Naval Weapons Station and Port Chicago Naval Magazine.",
